WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
OT telemetry is the foundation of visibility into industrial systems.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.750
It includes network communication, process values, device and controller events,

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.980
endpoint logs, alarms, identities, remote sessions, and configuration changes.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.380
Each source answers different questions and carries different limitations.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.545
Useful telemetry combines layers.

00:00:18.545 --> 00:00:21.070
Network data shows paths and protocol behavior.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.880
Process data shows physical conditions and control response.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.871
Endpoint and system logs identify users, files, services, and local changes.

00:00:27.871 --> 00:00:30.150
Protocol context explains industrial operations,

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.440
while asset and maintenance context explains why they matter.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.070
Safe collection is essential.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.975
Passive observation and existing logs are often preferred near sensitive systems,

00:00:38.975 --> 00:00:42.760
and any new agent, query, or configuration should be tested with engineering.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.555
Visibility must not undermine reliability, availability, or process integrity.

00:00:47.555 --> 00:00:51.475
Quality requires completeness, accuracy, synchronized time, useful retention,

00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:54.120
normalization, asset mapping, and honest coverage.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.109
Blind spots and noisy data should be measured and managed.

00:00:57.109 --> 00:01:00.945
Collection alone is not success if teams cannot trust or interpret the result.

00:01:00.945 --> 00:01:04.615
Security operations use telemetry for detection, hunting, incident response,

00:01:04.615 --> 00:01:08.025
anomaly analysis, inventory, and vulnerability prioritization.

00:01:08.025 --> 00:01:11.485
The strongest programs connect those workflows with operators and engineers,

00:01:11.485 --> 00:01:13.030
turn findings into improvements,

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.446
and continually align evidence with the real architecture.

00:01:15.446 --> 00:01:18.320
OT telemetry does not replace operational judgment;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.650
it gives that judgment a stronger factual foundation.
